* (x) 42.1. [feature] Authentication {* 42.1}

  Signup, login, OAuth, and two-factor authentication across all
  platforms. Supports email/password and social sign-in with optional
  TOTP-based 2FA.

  Pre-requisites:
  - (x) {* 42.6.3} Database — user tables
  - (x) {* 42.6.4} Cache — session store and rate limiting
  - (x) {* 42.6.7} Secrets — OAuth client credentials


** (x) 42.1.1. Stage 1 — Signup & Login {* 42.1.1}

*** (x) 42.1.1.1. Design {* 42.1.1.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a new user, I want to create an account with my email and a
      password, so that I can access the application on any device./
    - /As a returning user, I want to log in and have my session persist
      across app restarts, so that I don't re-authenticate constantly./

    Artifacts:
    - Registration and login flow diagrams
    - Database schema: `users`, `sessions`, `email_verifications` tables
    - API contract: OpenAPI spec for auth endpoints

*** (x) 42.1.1.2. Implementation {* 42.1.1.2}

**** (x) 42.1.1.2.1. Backend {* 42.1.1.2.1}
     - (x) User registration endpoint with email verification
       - AC: returns 201 + sends verification email within 5s
       - AC: 409 on duplicate email with descriptive error
       - AC: password stored as bcrypt hash (cost factor 12)
     - (x) Login endpoint with credential validation
       - AC: returns JWT access token (15min) + refresh token (30d)
       - AC: 401 on invalid credentials; no distinction between wrong
             email vs wrong password (prevents enumeration)
     - (x) Email verification flow with time-limited tokens
       - AC: token expires after 24h; single-use
       - AC: resend throttled to 1 request per minute per email
     - (x) Session management with refresh token rotation
       - AC: refresh tokens are single-use; rotation creates new pair
       - AC: old refresh token revoked immediately on use
     - (x) Rate limiting on auth endpoints
       - AC: 5 attempts/min per IP on login; 3/min on registration
       - AC: 429 response with `Retry-After` header
     - (x) Password reset flow (request + reset)
       - AC: reset link expires after 1h; invalidates previous links
       - AC: confirms success even for non-existent emails (no enumeration)

**** (x) 42.1.1.2.2. Frontend {* 42.1.1.2.2}
     - (x) Registration form with real-time validation
       - AC: email format check, password strength meter (zxcvbn)
       - AC: inline error messages; disabled submit until valid
     - (x) Login form with remember-me option
       - AC: stores refresh token in httpOnly cookie when checked
       - AC: auto-redirects to dashboard if already authenticated
     - (x) Email verification landing page
       - AC: success / expired / invalid states with appropriate messaging
       - AC: resend option on expired state
     - (x) Password reset flow (request form + new password form)
       - AC: email sent confirmation shown regardless of account existence
       - AC: new password form validates strength before submission
     - (x) Auth state context provider
       - AC: token refresh transparent to user; no flash of logged-out state
       - AC: auto-logout with redirect on session expiry

**** (x) 42.1.1.2.3. Mobile {* 42.1.1.2.3}
     - (x) Registration screen with platform-native form
       - AC: keyboard avoidance; haptic feedback on validation errors
       - AC: matches design system from {* 42.8.2}
     - (x) Login screen with biometric option
       - AC: Face ID / fingerprint after first successful login
       - AC: fallback to password if biometric fails 3 times
     - (x) Secure token storage (Keychain / Keystore)
       - AC: tokens encrypted at rest; cleared on logout
       - AC: survives app updates; does not survive app uninstall
     - (x) Deep link handling for email verification
       - AC: opens app from email link; falls back to web if not installed
     - (x) Session persistence across app restarts
       - AC: auto-login if valid refresh token exists
       - AC: re-prompts biometric if app was backgrounded >15min

*** (x) 42.1.1.3. Verification {* 42.1.1.3}
    - Backend: 8 test suites (registration, login, password reset,
      email verification, session refresh, rate limiting, token rotation)
    - Frontend: 5 test suites (forms, validation, auth state, redirects,
      error handling)
    - Mobile: 6 test suites (screens, biometric, secure storage, deep links,
      session persistence)
    - Integration: E2E auth flow — register → verify → login → refresh →
      logout across web and mobile

*** (x) 42.1.1.4. Validation {* 42.1.1.4}
    Outcome: signup completion rate >70%; email verification rate >85%
    - (x) 8 QA test scenarios (signup, login, reset, verify, biometric,
          session expiry, rate limiting, remember-me)
    - (x) REST acceptance scripts for all auth endpoints
    - (x) Security review: credential storage, token handling, enumeration
          prevention, rate limiting effectiveness


** (x) 42.1.2. Stage 2 — OAuth & Two-Factor {* 42.1.2}

*** (x) 42.1.2.1. Design {* 42.1.2.1}
    User stories:
    - /As a user, I want to sign in with my Google or Apple account, so
      that I can skip password creation and get started faster./
    - /As a security-conscious user, I want to enable two-factor
      authentication, so that my account is protected even if my password
      is compromised./

    Pre-requisites:
    - (x) {* 42.1.1} Stage 1 — Signup & Login

*** (x) 42.1.2.2. Implementation {* 42.1.2.2}

**** (x) 42.1.2.2.1. Backend {* 42.1.2.2.1}
     - (x) OAuth provider integration (Google, Apple)
       - AC: callback URL validated; state parameter prevents CSRF
       - AC: new user auto-created on first OAuth login
       - AC: existing user linked if email matches verified account
     - (x) TOTP-based two-factor authentication
       - AC: standard 6-digit code; 30s window with ±1 step tolerance
       - AC: setup requires verification of first code before enabling
     - (x) Backup recovery codes (10 codes, one-time use)
       - AC: generated on 2FA enable; stored as bcrypt hashes
       - AC: regeneration invalidates entire old set
     - (x) 2FA enforcement policy (configurable per organisation)
       - AC: grace period (7d default); hard enforcement after deadline
       - AC: admin can exempt specific users
     - (x) Session upgrade on 2FA completion
       - AC: session gains `2fa_verified` flag; flag expires after 30min
             for sensitive operations (password change, 2FA disable)

**** (x) 42.1.2.2.2. Frontend {* 42.1.2.2.2}
     - (x) OAuth sign-in buttons with provider branding
       - AC: follows Google/Apple brand guidelines; loading state on click
     - (x) 2FA setup wizard with QR code
       - AC: displays QR + manual entry key; validates test code before save
     - (x) 2FA code input with auto-submit
       - AC: 6 individual input boxes; auto-submits on last digit
       - AC: paste support for full 6-digit code
     - (x) Recovery code display and download
       - AC: shown once on enable; download as .txt; confirmation checkbox
     - (x) Account security settings page
       - AC: shows 2FA status, linked OAuth providers, active sessions
       - AC: revoke individual sessions; unlink OAuth providers

**** (x) 42.1.2.2.3. Mobile {* 42.1.2.2.3}
     - (x) OAuth sign-in via system browser
       - AC: uses ASWebAuthenticationSession (iOS) / Custom Tabs (Android)
       - AC: returns to app after auth; no WebView
     - (x) 2FA code input with clipboard detection
       - AC: detects OTP from authenticator app; offers auto-fill
     - (x) Push-based 2FA approval (approve/deny notification)
       - AC: shows request details (device, location); expires after 60s
       - AC: deny blocks login and alerts user
     - (x) Biometric re-auth for security settings
       - AC: required before viewing recovery codes or disabling 2FA

*** (x) 42.1.2.3. Verification {* 42.1.2.3}
    - Backend: 6 test suites (OAuth flow, TOTP, recovery codes, enforcement,
      session upgrade, provider linking)
    - Frontend: 5 test suites (OAuth buttons, 2FA wizard, code input,
      recovery codes, security settings)
    - Mobile: 4 test suites (OAuth browser, clipboard detection, push 2FA,
      biometric re-auth)
    - Integration: E2E OAuth + 2FA flow across platforms

*** (x) 42.1.2.4. Validation {* 42.1.2.4}
    - (x) 6 QA test scenarios (Google OAuth, Apple OAuth, 2FA setup,
          recovery code login, push approval, enforcement policy)
    - (x) Security review: OAuth state handling, TOTP timing, recovery
          code storage, session upgrade expiry
